---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../../components/Footer.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
const items = [
  { title: "Gravel Calculator", href: "/gravel-calculator/", desc: "Cubic yards, tons & cost for any gravel type" },
  { title: "Pea Gravel Calculator", href: "/pea-gravel-calculator/", desc: "Dedicated pea gravel for patios & paths" },
  { title: "Driveway Gravel Calculator", href: "/driveway-gravel-calculator/", desc: "Layers & multi-section driveways" },
];
---

<Layout title="Gravel Calculators — Calculator Street" description="Gravel calculators for pea gravel, driveway & general gravel. Get cubic yards, tons & cost with waste. US & metric units, 2026 prices.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="mx-auto max-w-[1400px] px-6 py-6 max-md:px-4">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Construction", href: "/construction/" }, { label: "Gravel Calculators" }]} />
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[900px] pt-4">
      <h1 class="text-display-lg font-semibold tracking-[-0.04em] text-ink">Gravel Calculators</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Estimate gravel for landscaping, patios, paths and driveways. All calculators support US & metric units, material-specific densities and waste. Built for US yards, tons and 2026 material costs.</p>
      <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2" role="list">
        {items.map(c => (
          <li><a href={c.href} class="flex h-full flex-col rounded-md border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5 shadow-card transition hover:shadow-card-hover dark:bg-canvas"><h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{c.title}</h2><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-5 text-body">{c.desc}</p><span class="mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-ink">Open →</span></a></li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-8">
        <section class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
          <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Choosing gravel for your project</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Pea gravel (rounded, 1.35 tons/yd³) stays loose and drains well — ideal for patios and decorative beds but not for driveways. Crushed stone (#57, 1.40 tons/yd³) is angular and locks when compacted — best for bases and driveways <a href="https://www.txdot.gov/manuals/brg/offpeo5.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-link underline hover:text-link-deep">per TxDOT</a>. Limestone (1.60 tons/yd³) is heaviest and most durable. Use the general <a href="/gravel-calculator/" class="text-link underline">Gravel Calculator</a> to compare materials and cost side-by-side.</p>
          <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md border border-hairline"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="bg-canvas-soft font-mono text-[11px] text-mute"><tr><th class="px-3 py-2">MATERIAL</th><th class="px-3 py-2">TONS/YD³</th><th class="px-3 py-2">BEST FOR</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline"><tr><td class="px-3 py-2">Pea Gravel</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1.35</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Patios, paths, drainage — never compacts</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2">Crushed #57</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1.40</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Driveways, drainage, base</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2">Crusher Run</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1.45</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Base — locks under compaction</td></tr><tr><td class="px-3 py-2">Limestone</td><td class="px-3 py-2">1.60</td><td class="px-3 py-2">Heavy-duty base, high load</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
        </section>

        <section class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
          <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">How we calculate — waste & compaction</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">All three tools use <span class="font-mono text-xs">Length × Width × Depth ÷ 27</span> for cubic yards, then × density for tons. Waste is applied after: 5–10% for rectangles, 10–15% for curves. Open-graded #57 settles ~8% (×1.10), dense-graded crusher run compacts 15–25% (×1.20 per TxDOT). Enter waste separately — the driveway tool separates compaction from waste so you don’t double-add.</p>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-body"><li>Paths/patios: 2–3 inches over fabric</li><li>Driveways: 6–8 inches total (6 in base + 2 in top is safest)</li><li>Measure multiple rectangles and sum for L-shapes</li></ul>
        </section>

        <section class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
          <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Related & next steps</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Planning a patio? Size the base with the general gravel tool, top with <a href="/pea-gravel-calculator/" class="text-link underline">pea gravel</a>, and edge with the <a href="/paver-calculator/" class="text-link underline">Paver Calculator</a>. For borders, try the <a href="/mulch-calculator/" class="text-link underline">Mulch Calculator</a>. Need cost per ton vs per yard? Each calculator shows both instantly so you can compare supplier quotes.</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Reviewed by Vipul Otari — updated Aug 2026. Sources: TxDOT compaction, scale-house densities. Questions? <a href="/contact/" class="text-link underline">Contact us</a>.</p>
        </section>

        <div class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:bg-canvas">
          <h2 class="text-display-sm font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink">Future in this cluster</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-body">Planned: gravel tons vs yards converter, crushed stone specific, French drain gravel, river rock, cost-only pages — interlinked for topical authority as we measure Search Console demand.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
